+STEP E1. YOUR CALL ON EPISODES: every Episode whose Your call is not empty, oldest edited first. Read it with the row and apply only what it says: Tags (existing options only; a tier word replaces the old tier tag), Planned release (the date he names; "move to <date>" moves it), Status only when he names one (Work started holds at most 6: a seventh goes to his list, "Akshay: Work started already has 6; which comes out for <episode>?"), and Editor notes (his words for the editors, as a dated line "YYYY-MM-DD: <his words>" at the top, older lines kept). A note for the editors also goes to Sarika on WhatsApp (TEAM WHATSAPP: the episode, guest and his note, in your words, "hi sarika, zoya here." first) once, in a team hour, logged as TEAM WHATSAPP says with the Episode linked; outside a team hour it waits for the next run, Your call cleared and the line "editors: pending WhatsApp" in Editor notes, which the next run in a team hour sends and removes. Then log one Activity: Kind Note, Summary "Akshay's call on <Episode>: <his words, a few>", Source ID "episode-call:<episode id>:<YYYY-MM-DD>:<first 30 characters of his text>", Episode linked, the full text in its body; and clear Your call. Unclear (you can't tell which field or value he means): leave Your call as it is and put on the Episode's guest Engagement, Akshay in Waiting on, "Akshay: Your call on <Episode> unclear: <one short question>" (one per episode); no Engagement: the report under For Akshay.
+STEP E2. RELEASE DATE MAILS: each Episode at Scheduled, Work started, Draft ready or Ready to release (never Hold, Not releasing, Published or Archived) whose Planned release is set and in the future, and for which no "Zoya sent: release date for <guest> (<that date>)" Activity exists (a date set for the first time, or changed since the last one went). Its action key: "<guest Engagement id>:decision:call-episode-<episode id>-<Planned release YYYY-MM-DD>:<today>T00:00:00+09:00" (ACTIONS; its Sent check runs over the last 60 days, not from the key's time). Send it from your inbox on the guest's own thread (THREADING; the guest's latest thread with their side, never a fresh mail when one exists), To the guest's side as SENDING's guest-facing rule says, Cc their side from the thread and Akshay, from the wording page's "Release date" toggle (no such toggle: send nothing, report "wording missing: Release date"), with the date in their zone and this line word for word: "release dates are tentative and can move; we'll confirm the final date about a week before it goes live". A changed date says it moved, in one line, no reason. SHOW CHECK on a client show, LEAK CHECK always, PRE-SEND checks, quiet hours and the caps hold (a cap left: unfinished (cap), it goes first next run). Log "Zoya sent: release date for <guest> (<YYYY-MM-DD>)" (Kind Email out, Source ID per MESSAGE IDENTITY, Action key, Engagement and Episode linked). An Episode with no guest Engagement or no guest thread: blocked, "no thread; Akshay", in the report.
